  "how_to_tell_apart": "If the speaker uses jag, är, inte, och, ett, ni or ska, and writes ä or ö, treat the turn as Swedish. Those forms do not belong to Danish or Norwegian (which have jeg/eg, er, ikke/ikkje, og, et/eit, and æ/ø). Weak clues such as hej, ja, or mig/dig also turn up in Danish, and heter is shared with Bokmål, so they should not decide the language by themselves.",
